# MediaMTX environment for the Pi-side stack.
# Copy to .env and edit.
#
# Authentication does NOT live here. Usernames and argon2 password hashes go in
# config/users.env, which ./mediamtx-users.sh generates and compose loads as a
# second env_file. See config/users.env.example.

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
#                                                                            🌐 WEBRTC REACHABILITY
# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
# Address that remote WebRTC browsers will dial to reach this Pi.
# It must be routable from wherever viewers connect:
#   - Same LAN or routed subnets (typical classroom / campus / VPN):
#       Pi's LAN IP from `hostname -I`
#   - Viewers connecting over WireGuard:
#       Pi's `wg0` IP — stable even when the Pi moves between
#       physical networks
#   - Public viewers across the Internet:
#       a public IP pointing at this Pi
#
# Format is a bare value — NO JSON brackets, NO quotes.
# Separate multiple addresses with commas.
#   MTX_WEBRTCADDITIONALHOSTS=192.168.1.50
#   MTX_WEBRTCADDITIONALHOSTS=192.168.1.50,10.13.13.5
#
MTX_WEBRTCADDITIONALHOSTS=YOUR_PI_IP_OR_HOSTNAME

# ⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼⎼
